Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
8 x+\left(6 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(6 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(8 x\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{8 x}{6 y}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{-32}{-12}=- \frac{8}{3}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=- \frac{8}{3}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(-2\right)&=- \frac{8}{3}\left(x-\left(-4\right)\right) \\
y&=- \frac{8}{3}\left(x-\left(-4\right)\right)+\left(-2\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=- \frac{8}{3}\left(x-\left(-4\right)\right)+\left(-2\right) \\
x-\left(-4\right)&=-\frac{-2}{- \frac{8}{3}} \\
x&=- \frac{19}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(- \frac{19}{4},0\right)$.

